{"id": "EUVD-2026-82191", "enisaUuid": "e9fc7eed-855e-3353-a469-8d4c846df4c1", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfirmware: arm_scmi: Fix SCMI device destroy lifetimes\n\nscmi_child_dev_find() drops the reference returned by\ndevice_find_child() before returning the scmi_device pointer. A\nconcurrent unregister can then release the device while the destroy path\nis still using the returned pointer.\n\nMake the lookup helper return the device_find_child() reference and keep\nit until scmi_device_destroy() has finished unregistering the child.\n\nAlso split device_unregister() in __scmi_device_destroy() so the SCMI bus\nID is not made reusable until after device_del() has removed the old\nscmi_dev.N name from sysfs. This avoids a new SCMI device reusing the\nsame ID while the old device is still registered.\n\nThe final device release callback is also a possible cleanup path when\nSCMI children are deleted by driver core recursion rather than\n__scmi_device_destroy(). Release the SCMI bus ID from a common helper\nused by destroy, register-failure and final-release paths, and clear\nscmi_dev->id after freeing it so the final release cannot free the same\nID again.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:11:01", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:51:49", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d8ecdceeb90cd2c265b222a7b65487faf68fea73", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/916e27f71a80f6d77c48d1a1a5782d6d5ef9017c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a60bc2df2d323cc1342f0cf95563cae266801e20", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c59b3393df1348a12308aaabd5fbc58ed6b21cf5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6abe8fe36b29ff51d1a42c2f338972883f4751a5"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93081", "GHSA-x6gc-qjww-67r2"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "21f9e02c-c298-3735-bf8f-167749f8d6fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "3651284a-4c21-3f27-82b0-dae6d1881fd9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1.138 <6.2"}, {"id": "41ab4ecd-41bb-31e7-9880-9e95616fce07", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "91ff1e9652fb9beb0174267d6bb38243dff211bb"}, {"id": "41f5b80b-33ab-3d3e-8999-c76138112764", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15.182 <5.16"}, {"id": "48bff1da-854e-37ac-a696-c82204bdf7ea", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "50569d41-6119-39bf-b8b7-81a764bceed5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "969d8beaa2e374387bf9aa5602ef84fc50bb48d8 <916e27f71a80f6d77c48d1a1a5782d6d5ef9017c"}, {"id": "652f969a-84b7-3fb0-b107-74b9263e57d8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.14.6 <6.15"}, {"id": "74195819-fc5e-38e3-8d98-801def66d988", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.90 <6.6.160"}, {"id": "77cbdec0-3834-3828-bda6-4c3b97eef24f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.15"}, {"id": "7a7ef79b-196f-38e9-a8c8-0a9033a09e35", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.28 <6.12.114"}, {"id": "7c55f715-7f6b-393d-aaf5-0e24d3a0bce6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9ca67840c0ddf3f39407339624cef824a4f27599 <6abe8fe36b29ff51d1a42c2f338972883f4751a5"}, {"id": "7c896884-0ec6-3a96-ad3e-ea8b96aac76a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9ca67840c0ddf3f39407339624cef824a4f27599 <c59b3393df1348a12308aaabd5fbc58ed6b21cf5"}, {"id": "80e8adb4-d1ee-3245-8ed0-25b40b81ffd3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9ca67840c0ddf3f39407339624cef824a4f27599 <a60bc2df2d323cc1342f0cf95563cae266801e20"}, {"id": "a3b8bebc-0e29-3d4e-b352-88767928ba3b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "df3c8749-8b1f-3ad3-b712-27dd6139f687", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "e1cc6cc0-dfb3-3206-82c1-c21685d87b3c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2fbf6c9695ad9f05e7e5c166bf43fac7cb3276b3 <d8ecdceeb90cd2c265b222a7b65487faf68fea73"}, {"id": "ed3b87e0-21f7-30c3-9d46-6c2ceb252f10", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "edb81eff-5b4e-3ce4-8d1b-6c387bd8206d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ff4273d47da81b95ed9396110bcbd1b7b7470fe8"}, {"id": "f452f04f-fd91-3e69-a3fe-a90644e32037", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8a8a3547d5c4960da053df49c75bf623827a25da"}, {"id": "f9464777-69cc-370d-9ac4-5619c8a70f6b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "edc4a4b7-359f-351f-9dd0-c4d1ae83e37c", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}